title: ch2_agency_leads
---
You have two ways to find clients this month. Paid ads on a professional network, or asking happy clients for referrals. #line:ch2_agency_leads_01
The ads promise leads at forty dollars each. Referrals cost a thank-you dinner. #line:ch2_agency_leads_02
-> Run the ads and track every dollar. #line:ch2_agency_leads_03
    <<choose "ads">>
    Twelve calls, two clients. Now you know exactly what one costs. #line:ch2_agency_leads_04
-> Ask your best clients for introductions. #line:ch2_agency_leads_05
    <<choose "referrals">>
    Slower, but the new clients already trust you. #line:ch2_agency_leads_06
===

title: ch2_agency_scope
---
A bakery client loves the chatbot you built. Now they want it to take orders, manage stock and post on social media. #line:ch2_agency_scope_01
For the same price, of course. #line:ch2_agency_scope_02
-> Send a new quote for the extra work. #line:ch2_agency_scope_03
    <<choose "quote">>
    They grumble, then sign. Clear scope, clear money. #line:ch2_agency_scope_04
-> Say yes to keep them happy. #line:ch2_agency_scope_05
    <<choose "yes">>
    You work three weekends for free. They tell everyone how flexible you are. #line:ch2_agency_scope_06
===

title: ch2_agency_late
---
A real estate firm owes you four thousand dollars. The invoice is forty days old. Rent is due Friday. #line:ch2_agency_late_01
-> Call them and agree on a date. #line:ch2_agency_late_02
    <<choose "call">>
    Half now, half in two weeks. You also add a late fee clause to every new contract. #line:ch2_agency_late_03
-> Wait politely. They're a big client. #line:ch2_agency_late_04
    <<choose "wait">>
    You put rent on a credit card. They pay in month three. #line:ch2_agency_late_05
===

title: ch2_agency_privacy
---
A clinic wants a bot trained on its patient emails. Faster, they say. Nobody will know. #line:ch2_agency_privacy_01
-> Refuse and propose a version without private data. #line:ch2_agency_privacy_02
    <<choose "refuse">>
    It takes longer. Their lawyer later thanks you in writing. #line:ch2_agency_privacy_03
-> Do it their way and bill them. #line:ch2_agency_privacy_04
    <<choose "do">>
    The invoice clears. You stop sleeping well. #line:ch2_agency_privacy_05
===

title: ch2_agency_tools
---
Your AI tool subscriptions crept up to six hundred dollars a month. Half of them you opened twice. #line:ch2_agency_tools_01
-> Cancel everything you don't use weekly. #line:ch2_agency_tools_02
    <<choose "audit">>
    Three hundred a month back. Nothing breaks. #line:ch2_agency_tools_03
-> Keep them. You might need them. #line:ch2_agency_tools_04
    <<choose "keep">>
    You might. The bill definitely needs you. #line:ch2_agency_tools_05
===

title: ch2_agency_pitch
---
A grocery chain with twelve stores invites you to pitch. They want automated inventory alerts. #line:ch2_agency_pitch_01
-> Spend a week building a working demo. #line:ch2_agency_pitch_02
    <<choose "prep">>
    The demo flags a real shortage live in the meeting. You win the contract. #line:ch2_agency_pitch_03
-> Pitch with slides and promises. #line:ch2_agency_pitch_04
    <<choose "slides">>
    They thank you politely and pick the team with a demo. #line:ch2_agency_pitch_05
===
